{
  "slug": "vibe-doc",
  "name": "Vibe Doc",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Vibe Doc is an AI-powered documentation gap analyzer for any codebase. It scans your project's artifacts, classifies the project type (web app, API, data pipeline, Claude Code plugin, etc.), measures coverage against a tier-appropriate documentation matrix, and either generates the missing docs from your existing artifacts or hands you a ranked list of gaps to close. Five slash commands cover the loop: /vibe-doc:scan (analyze), /vibe-doc:generate (write missing docs), /vibe-doc:check (CI deployment-readiness gate), /vibe-doc:status (snapshot), and /vibe-doc:evolve (Level-3 self-improvement — the plugin reads its own session logs and proposes SKILL improvements). Honest about coverage: no cherry-picked denominators, no false negatives the matcher has learned to flag.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills** and **5 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `check` (This skill should be used when the user mentions \"check my docs\", \"am I ready to deploy\", \"documentation…), `evolve-doc` (This skill should be used when the user says \\\"/evolve-doc\\\" or \\\"/vibe-doc:evolve-doc\\\" or wants Vibe Doc to reflect…), `friction-logger` (Internal SKILL — not a slash command), `generate` (This skill should be used when the user mentions \"generate docs\", \"write my documentation\", \"fix my gaps\", \"create…), `guide` (This skill provides shared behavior patterns, tone guidelines, and technical workflows used internally by other Vibe Doc skills), `scan` (This skill should be used when the user mentions \"scan my project\", \"check my documentation\", \"run vibe doc\",…), `session-logger` (Internal SKILL — not a slash command)\n- **Commands** (5): `check` (Check documentation completeness for deployment), `evolve-doc` (Reflect on past Vibe Doc sessions and propose plugin improvements), `generate` (Generate missing documentation), `scan` (Scan your project for documentation gaps), `status` (Show current Vibe Doc status)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install vibe-doc@claude-community` from `estevanhernandez-stack-ed/Vibe-Doc` (`packages/vibe-doc`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
